    <briefdescription>
<para>Cache-line aligned atomic counter. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Prevents false sharing in multi-threaded environments where multiple threads update separate counters. Each counter occupies its own cache line.</para>
<para>False sharing occurs when:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Two threads update variables in the same cache line</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>CPU must invalidate/synchronize the entire cache line</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Performance degrades due to cache coherency traffic</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Solution: Align each counter to cache line boundary (64 bytes) </para>
    </detaileddescription>
